<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George II of Great Britain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1683">1683</a>–<a href="/years/1760">1760</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a> and Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> from 1727 to 1760. He was the last British monarch to lead an army in battle, at Dettingen in 1743. In his reign <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>, the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> was chartered in his name, and he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-gottingen">University of Göttingen</a> in Hanover.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-ii-of-great-britain.jpg" alt="George II of Great Britain" width="320" height="528" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Hudson · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_II_by_Thomas_Hudson.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
